  "text_content": "Menu Student Files Classes Instructor Open submenu Reports Open submenu Set Class Schedule School Permits Close submenu Instructor Instructor Schedule Open submenu Instructor Reports Open submenu My Signatures Close submenu Instructor Schedule Booked Appointments Specify Hours Close submenu Instructor Reports Work Summary To Do Lists Close submenu Reports AQTR Registrations Ilan Preisler logout Self-Evaluation of In-Car Session Practical Session #5 Yap, Celine 1. In the Learner's view, what are the strengths and what are the weaknesses to be worked on at this stage of he practical training? Preparing to change lane (anticipation). Stop sign distance. 2. In the Instructor's view, what are the strengths and what are the weaknesses to be worked on at this stage of he practical training? Good basic control of vehicle. You need to do mirror checks more frequently. To work on lifting eyes up and scanning further ahead. This will give you more time to analyze the situation and come up with a plan of action. Try to practice more on multi-lane roadways and in denser traffic. Need to practice parking. Student Student Signature Yap, Celine Dec 12, 2025 Instructor Instructor Signature Anatoli Touranski L-XXX Save",
